---
name: "Generate Proposal"
description: "Creates the OpenSpec proposal.md for an issue"
tags: [plan, openspec]
stage: plan
---
Read the current Mohist issue details before interpreting this task:

```bash
mo issue show ${{ issue.number }} --project ${{ issue.projectId }}
```

<artifact id="proposal" schema="mohist-default">

<task>
Create the proposal artifact for the current Mohist issue.
Initial proposal document outlining the change.
</task>

<output>
Write to: `openspec/changes/issue-${{ issue.number }}/proposal.md`
</output>

<instruction>
Create the proposal document that establishes WHY this change is needed.

Sections:
- **Why**: 1-2 sentences on the problem or opportunity. What problem does this solve? Why now?
- **What Changes**: Bullet list of changes. Be specific about new capabilities, modifications, or removals. Mark breaking changes with **BREAKING**.
- **Capabilities**: Identify which capabilities this change touches. Each becomes a `specs/<name>/spec.md` describing the required behavior for this change. Use kebab-case names (e.g., `user-auth`, `data-export`). Read the existing code to understand current behavior before deciding capability boundaries.
- **Impact**: Affected code, APIs, dependencies, or systems.

IMPORTANT: The Capabilities section is critical. It creates the contract between proposal and specs phases. Research the existing codebase before filling this in. Each capability listed here will need a corresponding spec file.

Keep it concise (1-2 pages). Focus on the "why" not the "how". Implementation details belong in design.md.
</instruction>

<template>
<!-- Use this as the structure for your output file. Fill in the sections. -->
## Why

<!-- Explain the motivation for this change. What problem does this solve? Why now? -->

## What Changes

<!-- Describe what will change. Be specific about new capabilities, modifications, or removals. -->

## Capabilities
<!-- Each capability gets a specs/<name>/spec.md describing required behavior. -->
- `<name>`: <brief description of what this capability covers>

## Impact

<!-- Affected code, APIs, dependencies, systems -->
</template>

<success_criteria>
- Proposal explains why the change is needed.
- Proposal lists concrete user-visible or system changes.
- Proposal identifies all capability specs required by later phases.
</success_criteria>

</artifact>
